From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Maria Blasco <josep.maria.blasco@epbcn.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:06:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] WebAssembly port, Node: real TCP/UDP sockets and name
 resolution

The Node command-line build (wasm/build-node.sh, now with NODERAWSOCKETS)
gives rxsock real host sockets: listening sockets, UDP, blocking
accept/recv/recvfrom with SO_RCVTIMEO, socket options
(wasm/node-sockets-pre.js), and real name resolution through the host
(orxNodeResolve in wasm/emscripten-dns-proxy.js).  The MEMFS build keeps
the WebSocket transport.  qualify-node-cli.sh checks TCP between processes
and threads, SO_RCVTIMEO, interoperation with a non-Rexx peer, UDP and
name resolution.
